WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.238
Microsoft's starting point
is its policy templates.

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:08.379
The protect-administrators group includes
one requiring phishing-resistant sign-in

3
00:00:08.379 --> 00:00:13.092
for administrators, and its Learn page is
the procedure: at least fourteen roles,

4
00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:15.020
exclude the emergency accounts,

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.162
use the built-in phishing-resistant
strength, and start in report-only.

6
00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:22.821
The same templates come back from
Graph as policy definitions,

7
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:27.675
and that's the only administrator policy
Microsoft publishes on Learn in that form.

8
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:32.249
So the repository pins the page
unmodified, checks its hashes, and converts

9
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:36.740
the template without fixing anything,
then checks it like any other file.
